{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 44 (chapter 4, The Wild Heart): a drowned marsh under evening rain. Home isle southwest; two small reed isles east and north with a wolf den of four each; the seer isle and the ley isle further out; five causeways (rect aboveSea -8) join them only at low tide (from 40 s, every 120 s they rise to aboveSea 5 for 60 s, over 8 s, warned 10 s ahead). The aggressive eastern raiders and the turtle tribe in the north live on sheer plateaus (aboveSea 96 and 100, falloff 2) inside low rims, so neither can be reached until its stage raises a dry road and a stepped ramp. Stages: raise a Boathouse (start with 8 followers; until it stands, 4 raiders land on the home isle every 150 s from 300 s, the idle loss); clear both dens (clearDens n 2 without an area: the level has only these two dens); pray the dormant seer and ley stones until both are held; hold both 150 s (two posted keeper wardens spawn at each stone; 3 raiders land at the seer from 90 s and at the ley from 150 s, every 200 s, to pray them away); kill twelve of the eastern raiders after their road and ramp rise (a war band of 5 at 30 s, then 3 every 120 s, for the ley stone); take the north road and ramp and burn the walled Hearth (16 posted wardens, 3 towers, maxTroops 12; war bands of 4 for the seer every 150 s). From the dens on, neutral Mire swallows one causeway head every 160 s in turn, warned 10 s ahead, until the win. Hard bot offset 1 wins at tick 32406 (stages done at 2801, 11366, 14948, 17947, 24235); offsets 0 to 7 win 29550 to 35050. Time limit 3700 s (74000 ticks, over 2x the bot).",
